cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or contest this work, please cite the repository (below). Per-paper
  citation blocks live in each paper directory; cite the specific tagged release
  you examined so your critique targets a fixed version.
title: "U-Shares: Open Economic Research"
authors:
  - family-names: Blake
    given-names: Mike
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/U-Shares/u-shares-model"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"  # prose/figures: CC-BY 4.0 (see LICENSE.md)
abstract: >-
  Methods, formulas, directional findings, open questions, and a public claims
  register for U-Shares — a proposal to broaden capital ownership by converting
  part of an AI-driven growth dividend into ownership stakes ordinary households
  hold. Published to invite validation, calibration, and refutation; no program
  magnitude is asserted as established.
keywords:
  - citizen ownership
  - wealth distribution
  - universal basic capital
  - public finance
  - policy economics
# version + date-released + doi: stamped at each tagged release (Zenodo DOI minted per release).
